{
  "note": "Controlled tag vocabulary for per-quote tags. A quote's `tags` array holds these slugs, ordered most-specific-first; `scripts/validate_collections.py` rejects anything not listed here. `displayName` and `colorName` are what the app creates the tag as — without them an imported library mixes Title Case category tags with raw slugs in random colors. `useWhen` draws the boundary against the nearest neighbouring tag; read it before tagging. `avoid` lists spellings that must NOT be introduced as new tags — the validator points at this entry instead. An empty `tags: []` is not the same as no `tags` key: it records that the quote was read and deliberately left untagged, which is the honest outcome for a line famous for being iconic rather than for being about anything. Absent means the pass has not reached it yet.",
  "version": 4,
  "facets": {
    "theme": "What the quote is about. Every tagged quote needs at least one.",
    "occasion": "When you would actually reach for it. A claim about use, not topic.",
    "tone": "How it reads, and its form."
  },
  "budget": {
    "target": "3-5 tags per quote",
    "max": 6,
    "note": "The app's QuoteValidator.maxTagsPerQuote is 8 and the imported category tag takes one slot; 6 leaves headroom for a user's own tags."
  },
